{"step_index":276,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-26T06:17:41Z","thinking":"**Updating HTML Index**\n\nI've just added the script tag for `character-renderer.js`, ensuring it loads before `app.js`. Then, I swapped out those old, hardcoded image tags. Now, I'm using mount points instead, such as `<div id=\"bin-character-mount-lvl1\">`, to provide dynamic character rendering. This allows me to control character data directly from JavaScript, instead of directly editing html elements.\n\n\n**Expanding Mount Points**\n\nI've been creating mount points for levels 3, 5, 6, 7, and 8. Level 6 will showcase Bin looking out the window, and these are now placed next to the cloud frame. Also, I’m working on equipping the wardrobe in Level 1 with data attributes for different outfits: yellow/blue shirts, orange/blue shorts, and blue Velcro or white laced shoes. It will allow for dynamic customization.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"<!DOCTYPE html>\\n<html lang=\\\"vi\\\">\\n<head>\\n    <meta charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\">\\n    <meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, maximum-scale=3.0, user-scalable=yes, viewport-fit=cover\\\">\\n    <title>Cùng Bé Bin Đi Máy Bay (Parent-Co-Play Interactive Book)</title>\\n    <!-- Offline font fallback stack & Google Font -->\\n    <link rel=\\\"preconnect\\\" href=\\\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\\\">\\n    <link rel=\\\"preconnect\\\" href=\\\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\\\" crossorigin>\\n    <link href=\\\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Nunito:wght@700;800;900&display=swap\\\" rel=\\\"stylesheet\\\">\\n    <link rel=\\\"stylesheet\\\" href=\\\"css/style.css\\\">\\n</head>\\n<body>\\n    <div id=\\\"app-root\\\">\\n        <!-- Canvas Pháo hoa, Sao lấp lánh & Trái tim -->\\n        <canvas id=\\\"effects-canvas\\\"></canvas>\\n\\n        <!-- TOP BAR: 8 LEVEL DOTS & CỔNG BA MẸ -->\\n        <header class=\\\"top-nav